          "The book of Jeremiah does not present this catastrophe as a random event unrelated to the prophet’s earlier warnings. The destruction is connected to the people’s long history of covenant unfaithfulness, injustice and refusal to listen. Yet this theological explanation must not be used to claim that every modern war or disaster is a direct punishment from God. The text addresses a particular covenant relationship and a specific historical event.",
