          "Buying land at such a moment might have appeared foolish. Why invest in property when the land was threatened by conquest and the people faced exile? But Jeremiah carried out the purchase, arranged the legal documents and instructed Baruch to preserve them in a clay jar so they could last for a long time.",
          "The transaction became a prophetic sign. God declared that houses, fields and vineyards would again be bought in the land. The purchase expressed confidence that the devastation would not last forever.",
