          "The prophet’s hope was not built on the idea that Judah could avoid every consequence of its choices. It was grounded in the conviction that God could bring a future beyond the consequences.",
          "Jeremiah 33 continues the theme of restoration. It speaks of healing, peace, renewed joy and the return of thanksgiving. It also looks toward a righteous Branch from David’s line, connecting future hope with the promise of just leadership.",
