          "Success should produce gratitude, not arrogance. Achievement can tempt people to believe that they alone deserve the credit. Humility recognises the contributions of others and the limits of personal control.",
          "Authority comes with responsibility. Daniel’s warning connected the king’s conduct with righteousness and mercy toward the oppressed. Leadership should be measured partly by how it treats people who have less power.",
          "Listen to correction before the consequences become greater. Daniel warned Nebuchadnezzar before the dream’s judgment came to pass. Wise people take honest correction seriously rather than waiting for a crisis.",
          "No position makes a person beyond accountability. Nebuchadnezzar ruled a vast empire, but the biblical narrative insists that his authority was not ultimate. Leaders, professionals, parents and ministry workers must all remain accountable for their decisions.",
          "Restoration should lead to a changed perspective. At the end of the chapter, Nebuchadnezzar praises God rather than himself. Genuine humility involves more than feeling embarrassed; it changes how we understand our place and responsibilities."
